{"taskId":"grok-model-proof-45","requestedModel…26267 tokens truncated…s/baton/.baton/wt/grok-model-proof-composer/reviews/dogfood/grok-model-proof-composer.md","contents":"After reading GLOSSARY.md, the Baton concept that stood out most is the **Referee**—the feature where the fleet driver re-runs a worker's verification itself instead of trusting the worker's claim that tests passed. In a system built around directing Codex, Claude, and GLM harnesses, this is the mechanism that makes \"done\" mean something real rather than a self-reported status. It connects directly to hub-run verification (I7) and reflects Baton’s broader bet: orchestration value comes from independent checks, not from adding more scaffolding that a better model might route around.\n\nI was assigned the model identifier **grok-composer-2.5-fast** for this dogfood brief. The task was intentionally narrow—read the glossary, name the concept that mattered most, and record that identifier in a short review file without touching implementation code."}},"modelRequested":"grok-composer-2.5-fast","modelResolved":"grok-composer-2.5-fast","modelObserved":null,"seq":43,"ts":"2026-07-11T09:10:04.239Z"}
